WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.130
<b>Bell-mère</b>

38
00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.280
'Kay. So tell us all about it.
I gotta admit, I'm curious.

39
00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.060
– I'll pass.
– Hey, wait!

40
00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.220
[LUFFY] I don't care about her past.

41
00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.790
[SANJI] Where are you going, Luffy?

42
00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:03.900
[LUFFY] For a walk.

43
00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.130
[USOPP] A walk?!

44
00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:07.270
Do you mean you're not
gonna listen to this?!

45
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.520
[LUFFY] Nope.

46
00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.860
Who's he?

47
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:15.990
[ZORO] Don't mind him.
That's just how he is.

48
00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.110
We'll hear you out.
Though I can tell you right now,

49
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.150
I don't think it's
gonna change anything.

50
00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.240
Well, I'll listen too.

51
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.110
It might help me make some sense out
of everything that's going on around here.

52
00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.880
Me too! I wanna know all about her!

53
00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.800
[snoring]

54
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.130
Now he's asleep.

55
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.010
Hey, you said you'd hear her out!

56
00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:38.970
Mm. I see.

57
00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.060
This is why it was hard for her.

58
00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:48.980
I fell asleep.

59
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.860
Oh, no! Nojiko?

60
00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.700
I wonder where she ran off to.

61
00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.370
[NAMI] Just a little more, Bellemere.

62
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.900
Just a little more and
everything will be ours again.

63
00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:13.970
Cocoyashi Village,
the tangerine farm, everything!

64
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.230
[NAMI] It's taken eight years.

65
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.320
<b>Nami (8 Years Ago)</b>

66
00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:37.320
It's done!

67
00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.820
Yay! [laughing]

68
00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.870
Now if I could just get that book.

69
00:03:58.290 --> 00:03:59.430
Hey, is that you, Nami?

70
00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.260
Do you need any help there?

71
00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.220
[chuckles] No, I'm just looking.

72
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.060
I'll be going now.

73
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:10.860
[NAMI laughing nervously]

74
00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.730
Heh. That's too bad.

75
00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.740
[GENZO] Damn it, Nami! Not again!

76
00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:23.610
[VILLAGER A] Sticky fingers, eh, Nami?

77
00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.460
[NAMI] Let me go!

78
00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:27.460
I'm not a cat!

79
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:32.460
<b>Genzo (8 Years Ago)</b>

80
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.040
You little urchin!

81
00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:32.130
How many times do I have to tell
you that stealing is wrong?

82
00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.740
How else am I going to get what I need?

83
00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:35.960
I don't have any money.

84
00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.420
Cheapskate!

85
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.040
– [knocking]
– [GENZO] Bellemere!

86
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.090
Bellemere... I caught her stealing again.

87
00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.270
Now open up this door!

88
00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.900
<b>Bell-mère
Nami and Nojiko's
Foster Mother</b>

89
00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.860
[sighs] What do you want now?

90
00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.820
You're back. That was a quick trip.

91
00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:55.370
I got a ride.

92
00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.700
Listen, you better get control of her
before she winds up in a jail cell!

93
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.280
Thanks for the advice.

94
00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:06.120
Haven't you ever seen somethin'
you've wanted and just taken it?

95
00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.250
You're the reason she acts this way!

96
00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:09.870
[BELLEMERE] Relax, I'm just kidding.

97
00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.250
I hope you were
kind enough to pay for her.

98
00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.420
Uh, Bellemere.

99
00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:16.530
Thanks so much.

100
00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.330
I don't have the money right now.

101
00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.050
I'll pay you somehow.

102
00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:23.930
Does that sound good?

103
00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.220
[GENZO] You can't say things like that!

104
00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.890
[NAMI, BELLEMERE laughing]

105
00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.890
Look, he's as red as a beet.

106
00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.020
[BOTH laughing]

107
00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.980
[NAMI laughing]

108
00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.070
[BELLEMERE clears throat]

109
00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.900
Now then, laugh it up
while you still can, Nami.

110
00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.450
[NAMI] I'm sorry!

111
00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.200
It's just that I... I really
need that book, Bellemere.

112
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.580
Then why didn't you ask me
if I would buy it for you?

113
00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.080
[NAMI] Because I know you can't afford it.

114
00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:54.580
Of course I can.

115
00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.880
There's money left over
from the last harvest.

116
00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:59.010
But I heard them in the village.

117
00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:03.090
They said the weather's been so good lately
that everyone's tangerines will sell,

118
00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:06.720
which means we can't raise our price
or we may not be able to sell at all!

119
00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.850
[BELLEMERE] They don't know
what they're talking about.

120
00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:11.270
<b>Nojiko (8 Years Ago)</b>

121
00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.050
Way to go, Nami.

122
00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:14.050
If I had stolen it, there's
no way I would have been caught.

123
00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.400
– [thud, thud]
– [NAMI, NOJIKO] Ow!

124
00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.520
No more stealing, right?

125
00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.360
I was just joking, that's all.

126
00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.990
That really hurt.

127
00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:25.990
[laughing]

128
00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:32.330
I'm sorry. But one thing's for sure,
the maps you draw are so amazing, Nami.

129
00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.920
I see you can draw land maps
now as well as sea charts.

130
00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.800
[NOJIKO] That's a map
of our island, isn't it?

131
00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:46.220
Nobody will believe that such a little
girl drew this all by herself.

132
00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.390
[chuckles]

133
00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.720
I wanted the book so I'd be able
to start studying navigation.

134
00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.850
Navigation as well?

135
00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.690
You're gonna be a navigator?

136
00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.790
[NAMI] That's right, I'm going to guide
ships around all the oceans of the world.

137
00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:00.610
It'll be great!

138
00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:04.360
And I'll be able to make maps
of all the far-off places I'll go.

139
00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.660
[giggles]

140
00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:10.280
So, this island map is the first step
toward realizing your dream, is that it?

141
00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:12.370
[NAMI] Mm-hmm!

142
00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.540
[BELLEMERE] A world map, huh?

143
00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:17.790
Nami, your dream is going to come true.

144
00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.290
I have no doubt.

145
00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:30.970
– Hey, uh, Bellemere?
– [BELLEMERE] Hm?

146
00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.310
Why haven't you been
eating dinner with us lately?

147
00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.270
I've been eating tangerines.

148
00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:37.900
I've just been on a diet, that's all.

149
00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.190
[NOJIKO] Then I don't want to eat either.

150
00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.320
What's with all of the drama?

151
00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.570
You need to eat because
you are a growing girl.

152
00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.070
Why do you keep lying to us?

153
00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:50.280
You're not eating because we don't have
enough money to buy food. That's why.

154
00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:50.990
Really?!

155
00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.370
You're starving yourself
so that we won't go hungry.

156
00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:58.250
Tangerines replenish my skin with
the power of liquid sunlight.

157
00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.740
And they are the only reason I am still
such a ravishing beauty even though

158
00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.960
I am in my extreme late twenties.

159
00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:05.570
But your hands are all yellow.

160
00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:08.340
Would you just shut up
and eat your food already!

161
00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.140
And here you go, Nami! All done!

162
00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:13.850
A Bellemere one-of-a-kind original!

163
00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.890
Oh, great... a hand-me-down.

164
00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:18.190
Yeah, that's true. But it suits you.

165
00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:19.520
See, look.

166
00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.610
But the lion used to be a sunflower.

167
00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.230
Quit complaining.

168
00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:26.570
You have to take my hand-me-downs,
or you won't get any new clothes.

169
00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:30.740
But it's not fair. You get new clothes
all the time and mine are all used.

170
00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.740
I get old clothes too, ya know.

171
00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:35.290
So just suck it up, Nami,
and take what you get.

172
00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:36.790
Understand?

173
00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.330
We didn't come from
the same parents anyway.

174
00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:42.330
We're not real sisters, so who cares?!

175
00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:43.840
– [BELLEMERE] Nami!
– [thwack]

176
00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:52.850
Bellemere, please.

177
00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.310
So what if you don't
have the same parents.

178
00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.240
I don't ever want to hear you
say anything like that again.

179
00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.530
I... don't care...

180
00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.310
You're not even our real mother!

181
00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:14.710
You're just some lady
who's taking care of us!

182
00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:19.160
You wish we'd never come here so you
could buy clothes and food for yourself!

183
00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:21.620
You'd be better off
without us, wouldn't you!

184
00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.130
That way you could be selfish
and do whatever you want.

185
00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:28.920
I wish... I wish someone rich
would've adopted us

186
00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.090
instead of a stinky loser like you!

187
00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.020
[NAMI sobbing]

188
00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.940
Well... fine.

189
00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:46.480
If you hate it here so much, you can go
find someplace else to live if you want.

190
00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:47.900
I didn't sign up for this.

191
00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:49.860
Stop fighting! Please, just stop!

192
00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:52.740
I'm never coming back!

193
00:09:53.500 --> 00:09:56.780
[NOJIKO] Nami, stop! Nami!

194
00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.130
Bellemere... um...

195
00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:09.510
The three of us are a family.
That's the truth!

196
00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:14.260
And you know Nami feels the same...
no matter what she said.

197
00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.560
Look who's being the adult here.

198
00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.850
I blew up and you're
the level-headed one.

199
00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.480
Why don't you go and find Nami?

200
00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.480
I'll make something special for
dinner and we can all make up, okay?

201
00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:41.540
<b>Cocoyashi Village</b>

202
00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:44.460
Sorry, lady. Two for five is
the lowest price I can offer.

203
00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.650
[VILLAGER D] Is that really
your best offer?

204
00:10:47.650 --> 00:10:50.420
[VILLAGER F] Half off!
Today only! Fresh produce!

205
00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:52.970
[VILLAGER G] You won't find
a lower price anywhere today!

206
00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:55.590
I guarantee it or your money back.

207
00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:01.970
[GENZO laughing]

208
00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.520
[chuckles] So you've run away from home

209
00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.520
and come to the village.
Now what's the plan?

210
00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.280
Drink before it gets cold.

211
00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:19.620
Bellemere would be so much happier if
she didn't have to take care of us.

212
00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:21.950
And why would you say that?

213
00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.830
Well, you need a lot of money
to take care of two kids,

214
00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:29.210
and because of me, the whole
village hates her right now.

215
00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.590
[GENZO] That's progress.

216
00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.210
At least you're considering others.

217
00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:33.670
[chuckles]

218
00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.040
But don't worry,
when Bellemere was your age,

219
00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:39.080
she was a complete nightmare
terrorizing the entire village.

220
00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.600
Is that... the truth?

221
00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.060
[GENZO] Sure, even now
the villagers look at her

222
00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.890
– as some kind of a screw-up.
– [NAMI] Huh?

223
00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:48.400
So you can imagine how surprised
everyone in the village was

224
00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.650
when she joined up
with the Marines, huh?

225
00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:54.320
Marines? You mean
Bellemere was in the Marines?

226
00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:55.950
That's right.

227
00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:59.320
[MARINES, pirates yelling]

228
00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:05.830
[GENZO] She said she couldn't
stand by and do nothing

229
00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.460
while pirates killed innocent people.

230
00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:10.920
Then she left the village.

231
00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:22.350
[GENZO] She was teetering
on the verge of death when...

232
00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:28.270
[BELLEMERE] If this is
the end, then so be it.

233
00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:34.480
– [babbling]
– [BELLEMERE] Huh?

234
00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:38.450
[baby babbling]

235
00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:42.120
[BELLEMERE groaning]

236
00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.490
[baby babbling]

237
00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:47.000
[BELLEMERE] Your little sister?

238
00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:54.380
[NOJIKO] Mn-mm. I found her.

239
00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.140
[laughing]

240
00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:06.310
How did she survive?

241
00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:10.190
[NOJIKO sobbing]

242
00:13:10.190 --> 00:13:14.610
[laughing]

243
00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:21.320
[NOJIKO, BELLEMERE sobbing, laughing]

244
00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:24.070
[GENZO] That innocent child was you, Nami.

245
00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:30.040
And seeing how precious you were gave
Bellemere the right reasons to live again.

246
00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.440
[VILLAGER H] It is a ship! I knew it!

247
00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.850
[VILLAGER I] Who on earth would be out
in such a terrible storm?

248
00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:55.110
[VILLAGERS murmur]

249
00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.400
[BELLEMERE] Doctor! I need a doctor!

250
00:13:57.720 --> 00:14:00.650
What's going on?
What happened to you, Bellemere?

251
00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.490
Bellemere?!

252
00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.240
Did somebody call for a doctor?

253
00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.530
[DOCTOR] Whose are these children?

254
00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.290
Doctor! They're burning up.

255
00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:11.120
I'm afraid they might be really sick.

256
00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.080
Please, help them!

257
00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:13.330
[DOCTOR] Give them here.

258
00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.420
Alright. And we'd better mend up those
nasty wounds of yours as well, young lady.

259
00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.190
[BELLEMERE] Never mind me.

260
00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:25.510
Please, just don't let them die!
You have to save them!

261
00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:30.430
I'm begging you, Doctor!

262
00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:36.190
I don't believe it.
Say that whole thing again.

263
00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:39.110
I said I'm going to try to be
the mother of these two girls.

264
00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:40.150
It's that simple.

265
00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:41.400
No way!

266
00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:45.610
That's insane! You are far too immature
to handle this much responsibility.

267
00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:47.950
You can't handle them by yourself.

268
00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:49.660
Just hand them over to the author...

269
00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:51.290
– I've made my mind!
– [ALL yell]

270
00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.420
You can't deny that I'm an adult.

271
00:14:54.590 --> 00:14:55.790
And what I lived through as a Marine

272
00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:58.670
has given me the right to
be treated with more respect.

273
00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.510
I'm perfectly capable of taking
care of these two girls.

274
00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:06.930
And nothing can stop me from
raising them to be wonderful girls.

275
00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:10.470
So now we're going to be
a family together.

276
00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:13.770
Nami and Nojiko have
renewed my love of life.

277
00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:23.570
The bond between the three of you girls
goes far deeper than any "normal" family.

278
00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.910
Nami! I thought I'd find you here.

279
00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.860
Nojiko?

280
00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.250
Come on! Bellemere's waiting for us.

281
00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.620
She's making us a special supper.

282
00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.590
[gasps]
Sure!

283
00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.750
[NOJIKO] I think
she's making your favorite.

284
00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.840
– Omelets with tangerine sauce.
– [NAMI] Yay!

285
00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:45.510
[NAMI, NOJIKO giggle]

286
00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.550
– [NAMI] I love omelets!
– [NOJIKO] Alright!

287
00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.180
[NAMI, NOJIKO giggle]

288
00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.770
Pirates are coming! Everybody run!

289
00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:59.810
– [VILLAGERS screaming]
– [VILLAGER O] Pirates!

290
00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.940
[VILLAGER P] Quick,
the pirates are coming, hide!

291
00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:16.250
– The Arlong Pirates!
– Arlong?!

292
00:16:17.150 --> 00:16:19.370
– That's impossible.
– [VILLAGER T] Why would fishmen

293
00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:21.250
from the Grand Line come here?

294
00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:25.050
[VILLAGER U] The rumor about the split
between the Fishman Pirates must be true.

295
00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:26.550
[GENZO] Nami! Nojiko!

296
00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.670
[NAMI] Genzo!

297
00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.800
It's too dangerous for you here.
Go hide in the woods.

298
00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:32.970
But what about...?

299
00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.270
[GENZO] You must go! Now!

300
00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:41.770
[FISHMEN chattering]

301
00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:49.150
Greetings and salutations,
you pathetic little humans.

302
00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:54.400
From this moment on, this entire island and
its inhabitants are a part of my domain.

303
00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.250
[FISHMEN] Yeah!

304
00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.910
[ARLONG] Listen closely.

305
00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:02.920
From now on, the first day of every month
you will buy your lives from me!

306
00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:09.300
A hundred thousand berries for adults,
fifty thousand for children.

307
00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:11.720
Those who cannot pay... will die!

308
00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:13.470
[ARLONG laughs intensely]

309
00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:16.850
[NAMI] What should we do, Nojiko?

310
00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.070
We don't have that much money.

311
00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:21.600
Maybe the fishmen won't
be able to find our house.

312
00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.480
You can't see it from here.

313
00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:30.570
Is that it? So what's the haul?

314
00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:33.530
About twenty-five million, give or take.

315
00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:39.500
You all shall live!
[laughing]

316
00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:42.290
It looks like we each
have to pay 100,000 berries

317
00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:45.090
to these fishmen
every month just to stay alive!

318
00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:47.460
No, there's no way we could survive.

319
00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.720
We don't have a choice.
We should just be happy

320
00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:52.760
that nobody in the village
has been killed yet.

321
00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:57.680
[GENZO] If all they want is money,
that's an easy price to pay.

322
00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:01.440
I just hope they leave without
noticing Bellemere's house.

323
00:18:01.440 --> 00:18:04.730
With two children
she'd need 200,000 berries.

324
00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:08.820
There's no way she has that much saved.

325
00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:11.690
[ARLONG] It's time to leave.

326
00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.820
Come, brothers.

327
00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.780
[GENZO exhales]

328
00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:17.160
[NAMI sighs]

329
00:18:17.170 --> 00:18:20.620
[FISHMAN J] Arlong! There's smoke
coming from outside the village!

330
00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:21.960
[ARLONG] Huh?

331
00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:26.460
[BELLEMERE humming]

332
00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.870
Okay! Let's see...

333
00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:33.010
Delicious! There isn't anything quite
as tasty as my special tangerine sauce.

334
00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:35.970
Nami and Nojiko are gonna love it.

335
00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.890
It looks like chimney smoke
from somebody's house.

336
00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:44.270
Oh? We almost missed that one.

337
00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:46.150
[NAMI, NOJIKO] Bellemere.

338
00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:49.110
Alright! Let's go, guys. Heh.

339
00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:53.030
[VILLAGER X] This is bad!

340
00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:55.160
The pirates are going
to Bellemere's house.

341
00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.830
Genzo, look! Nojiko and Nami are gone!

342
00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:03.030
What did you say?!

343
00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:05.670
I think the duck
needs another ten minutes.

344
00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.290
And the stew is almost ready.

345
00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:12.130
This is definitely gonna blow my budget,
but sometimes you gotta live a little.

346
00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:19.220
[ARLONG chuckles]

347
00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.930
[NAMI] Bellemere...

348
00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:23.640
Bellemere!

349
00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:26.440
Bellemere's gonna be killed!

350
00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.570
[VILLAGER A] We will
not abandon Bellemere!

351
00:19:36.490 --> 00:19:39.160
[GENZO] Damn it, why did this happen!

352
00:19:39.160 --> 00:19:41.370
Hold on, Bellemere!

353
00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:46.120
Oh, they're here.

354
00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:57.590
[BELLEMERE] It's open! Come in!

355
00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:58.800
Why, thanks.

356
00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:26.080
[BELLEMERE] I guess you weren't
expecting a former Marine.

357
00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:32.540
Now what would a pirate from the
Grand Line want with Cocoyashi Village?

358
00:20:37.560 --> 00:20:38.430
What's so funny?

359
00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:40.890
Hahahahaha!

360
00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:42.760
[gasps]

361
00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:49.570
Useless... Foolish...
Stupid... Empty... Worthless.

362
00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:54.610
All of you humans... You have
no strength to speak of.

363
00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:59.860
Hahahaha!

364
00:21:01.350 --> 00:21:03.690
[NAMI] We'll help her
escape through the back door.

365
00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:05.760
What if the pirates are already there?

366
00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:06.690
[NAMI] It'll be okay.

367
00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:07.660
[DOCTOR] Stop!

368
00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:12.330
Doctor!

369
00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.040
You can't go back home.

370
00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:16.510
– [NOJIKO] What?
– But we have to save Bellemere!

371
00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:19.510
Nojiko, Nami...!
Quiet and listen to me...

372
00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:23.670
There will be times... times
in life like this moment now...

373
00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:27.680
when you have to learn the truth
no matter how hard it is to take.

374
00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:29.480
[NOJIKO] Doctor!

375
00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:31.230
[BELLEMERE screams]

376
00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.520
Bellemere, no!

377
00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:37.980
Auuuugh!

378
00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:42.820
[BELLEMERE] It's no use.

379
00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:46.990
These guys are real monsters
and I'm going to die.

380
00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.200
Nojiko. Nami.

381
00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:50.710
[GENZO] Bellemere!

382
00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:53.810
Don't waste your life
because you're a stubborn fool.

383
00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:55.480
There's no reason for this fight

384
00:21:55.480 --> 00:22:00.090
when it can be resolved with
a simple exchange of money.

385
00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:03.230
Just pay the fee, and I'll stop.

386
00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:06.970
A hundred thousand for each adult
and fifty thousand for each kid, if any.

387
00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:10.810
If you can pay for your whole family,
I'd gladly spare your lives.

388
00:22:10.810 --> 00:22:12.060
Family?

389
00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:16.650
How much money do you have...?

390
00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:18.690
You need two hundred thousand.

391
00:22:20.070 --> 00:22:21.700
I don't have it...

392
00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:22.900
I'm not even close.

393
00:22:25.280 --> 00:22:28.240
Hey, the table is
set for three in here.

394
00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:34.250
Oh, a family of three. Hahahaha!

395
00:22:34.430 --> 00:22:36.460
It's for me and my friend...

396
00:22:38.020 --> 00:22:43.130
[GENZO] We were supposed to have
a nice dinner tonight before you came.

397
00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:45.890
Come, Bellemere, I know you've
made something wonderful.

398
00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:48.350
Pay them before our food gets cold.

399
00:22:48.710 --> 00:22:49.310
Genzo.

400
00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:53.140
Just pay the pirates...
and then they'll leave us alone.

401
00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:56.690
Now everyone is saved.

402
00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:57.940
It's true...

403
00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:02.190
The village register shows no record
of her marrying or giving birth...

404
00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:04.070
She's always been single.

405
00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:09.440
Listen...

406
00:23:09.440 --> 00:23:13.030
There's no way that the pirates
will ever find out about you...

407
00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:15.920
But you have to leave
this island immediately...

408
00:23:15.930 --> 00:23:17.380
And don't ever look back.

409
00:23:18.070 --> 00:23:20.880
It's the only way for all
three of you to survive.

410
00:23:21.780 --> 00:23:23.840
We can't afford it any other way.

411
00:23:23.850 --> 00:23:25.920
You're much too young
to be at sea alone,

412
00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:29.030
but you've survived before
and if there's even a chance...

413
00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:29.720
[NAMI] No.

414
00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:30.600
[gasps]

415
00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:32.390
[NAMI] I don't want to.

416
00:23:32.820 --> 00:23:36.140
I... I want to stay in this village.

417
00:23:36.150 --> 00:23:38.960
It's because... we're poor.

418
00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:41.900
That's why we can't stay together.

419
00:23:42.430 --> 00:23:44.990
[NAMI] Why? Why can't they just go away?

420
00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:51.240
Well then... now we can all be safe.

421
00:23:51.820 --> 00:23:52.860
Fine, we'll leave this island.

422
00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:53.830
Nojiko.

423
00:23:53.920 --> 00:23:57.420
[NOJIKO] We have to leave
or Bellemere will die!

424
00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:16.390
[BELLEMERE] Wait!
Who said I was paying for me?

425
00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:20.230
That money I gave up was
for my two daughters...

426
00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:22.070
But I can't pay you.

427
00:24:22.570 --> 00:24:24.320
[gasps]

428
00:24:24.090 --> 00:24:24.780
[ARLONG] Hmmm?

429
00:24:24.320 --> 00:24:25.740
What are you doing?

430
00:24:26.110 --> 00:24:27.200
It's okay...

431
00:24:27.270 --> 00:24:30.320
I... have to do this for my family.

432
00:24:31.110 --> 00:24:33.030
Even if it costs me my life.

433
00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:36.500
Stupid girl.

434
00:24:36.550 --> 00:24:42.490
It's true the three of us aren't
related by blood, but we're family...

435
00:24:42.490 --> 00:24:45.130
All I've ever wanted
was to be their mother.

436
00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:49.630
And now... I can be.

437
00:24:51.070 --> 00:24:52.320
[NAMI, NOJIKO] Bellemere!

438
00:24:52.320 --> 00:24:55.220
I wish someone rich would've adopted us

439
00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:57.590
instead of a stinky loser like you!

440
00:24:57.590 --> 00:24:59.480
[NAMI] It was a lie!

441
00:24:59.630 --> 00:25:01.100
I was lying, Bellemere!

442
00:25:01.530 --> 00:25:03.820
[NOJIKO] Bellemere!

443
00:25:16.670 --> 00:25:18.240
Don't cry, girls...

444
00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:19.570
I wish I could have...

445
00:25:19.570 --> 00:25:22.340
I could have provided for you better...

446
00:25:22.340 --> 00:25:26.170
I wish... I could have been
a better mother to the both of you.

447
00:25:26.520 --> 00:25:27.510
Don't say that!

448
00:25:27.560 --> 00:25:29.380
[NAMI] We don't need anything,
just don't die!

449
00:25:29.390 --> 00:25:30.880
Don't ever leave us!

450
00:25:31.020 --> 00:25:34.180
[NAMI] You need to see the map I'm
going to draw of the whole world!

451
00:25:36.030 --> 00:25:37.600
Yes... your map...

452
00:25:38.340 --> 00:25:42.150
Go and make your dreams come true.

453
00:25:43.870 --> 00:25:45.570
For me.

454
00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:47.650
Bellemere, no!

455
00:25:50.080 --> 00:25:52.570
[ARLONG] So these are your daughters.

456
00:25:53.950 --> 00:25:54.820
[NOJIKO gasps]

457
00:25:55.120 --> 00:25:56.320
Yeah, that's right...

458
00:25:56.320 --> 00:25:59.500
And you have to promise me
that you'll leave them alone.

459
00:25:59.500 --> 00:26:02.830
No problem... as long as
you die like a good girl.

460
00:26:02.830 --> 00:26:03.420
Help us.

461
00:26:03.420 --> 00:26:04.630
[screams]

462
00:26:15.250 --> 00:26:16.650
Well then...

463
00:26:16.650 --> 00:26:21.390
Don't kill them, boys.
No, just teach them a lesson.

464
00:26:21.530 --> 00:26:24.350
Now to set an example.

465
00:26:27.200 --> 00:26:28.150
Ahh!

466
00:26:28.170 --> 00:26:31.400
Hmph! You ready to die?

467
00:26:41.460 --> 00:26:43.290
Nojiko... Nami!

468
00:26:46.350 --> 00:26:47.460
Love you...
